;
; DEED clause profile: (rsr-profile …) in <repo>_chora.deed, v1.1.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; section 10 (the check-rsr-profile.sh row) and ruling J39 of 2026-11-15 (one
; grammar owns the clause's keys; scripts/check-rsr-profile.sh and every other
; reader fail closed against it). Field source: the clause as the owner moved
; it from .machine_readable/rsr-profile.a2ml (2026-11-05), in
; rsr-template-repo_chora.deed and standards_chora.deed, and the fields
; check-rsr-profile.sh reads.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `clause` of
; deed.abnf v2.0.0, so a chora deed carrying it still passes deed_lint
; unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, keyword and token-sep are
; deed.abnf's; str-list and str-list1 are common.abnf's. Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..."
; case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: the top level of a <repo>_chora.deed (head repo-deed, and
; that file name: 0-AI-MANIFEST.deed is a repo-deed but never carries it), at
; most once (check-rsr-profile.sh refuses two). SEMANTIC (validator-enforced,
; deed_lint.js --rsr-profile):
;   * :version is present; every field at most once, inside (notes …) too;
;     (notes …) at most once;
;   * a non-empty :capabilities, a :preset, or both (an empty :capabilities
;     declares nothing, as check-rsr-profile.sh reads it);
;   * the strings are not empty; list items are not empty and appear once;
;   * no other field and no other clause: a reader that meets an unknown key
;     refuses the clause, never skips it (J39).
;   * (layout …) at most once, holding one or more (module :gate … :at …),
;     each with exactly one :gate and one non-empty :at; a :gate names one
;     module once; an :at path is repo-relative (no leading "/", no "." or
;     ".." segment, no "//") and concrete (no "*", "?", "[", "]" or "|"),
;     with a trailing "/" for a directory, and appears once in its module.
; Whether a capability or preset is known is the gate table's business
; (0-canon/template-capability-gates.toml), checked by check-rsr-profile.sh.

rsr-profile-clause = "(" %s"rsr-profile" 1*(token-sep rsr-profile-member) [token-sep] ")"
rsr-profile-member = ( %s":version"          token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":spec"             token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":declares-against" token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":role"             token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":preset"           token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":capabilities"     token-sep str-list )
                   / ( %s":add"              token-sep str-list )
                   / ( %s":remove"           token-sep str-list )
                   / rsr-profile-layout
                   / rsr-profile-notes
                   ; :spec names the criteria canon ("rsr-criteria-v2") and
                   ; :declares-against its version. :role is read by
                   ; check-rsr-profile.sh ("spine", "canon"); an unknown role
                   ; gets no carrier exemption there, so it stays a string.
                   ; Effective capabilities = :capabilities + the :preset's
                   ; + :add - :remove.

rsr-profile-notes  = "(" %s"notes" *(token-sep keyword token-sep string) [token-sep] ")"
                   ; Prose only, such as :omitted-rationale. Nothing in it is
                   ; read as a profile field: a :role inside (notes …) never
                   ; makes a repo a spine.

; (layout …), v1.1.0 (owner ruling 2026-11-16, rsr-template-repo#421): where
; THIS repo keeps a capability-gated module, so that the repo's layout and its
; check cannot drift apart. The gate table says WHAT a capability owes and
; where it lives by default; a (module …) binds one gate-table row to the
; paths this tree actually uses. :gate names the row by one of its
; alternatives exactly as the table writes it ("abi.ipkg"); :at lists the
; paths that replace the row's default locations. check-rsr-profile.sh
; requires every :at path to exist when the row's capability is declared, to
; be the same kind of artefact (same file name, or a matching name for a
; glob row; a directory for a directory row), reports a present one as
; VESTIGIAL when it is not declared, and fails a binding whose paths are gone.
; Whether a :gate names a real, bindable row is the gate table's business,
; checked there, as for capabilities.
rsr-profile-layout = "(" %s"layout" 1*(token-sep layout-module) [token-sep] ")"
layout-module      = "(" %s"module" 1*(token-sep layout-member) [token-sep] ")"
layout-member      = ( %s":gate" token-sep string )
                   / ( %s":at"   token-sep str-list1 )
